			Ah yes, the classic “I built my own because the SaaS was awful” origin story. I’ve heard that one three times now — first with expert systems in the ’90s, then with big data Hadoop clusters, then with blockchain “infrastructure.” Every time, someone rolls out a self-hosted demo that generates beautiful reports or spins up a slick Next.js site, and every time the conversation ends the same way: “Show me the prod deployment.” Because making a PDF that looks good is not a production system. Making a PowerPoint is not a production system. Building a full site from a prompt is a demo that breaks the moment the data is messy, the edge cases multiply, or the API rate limits kick in. I’m sure your “solid app” works great on your machine with your carefully curated test queries. It always does.

